From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Basem Barakat <basem.barakay@amd.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 19:53:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] [Core][Bugfix] Drop bounded_replay when promoting
 SlidingWindowMLASpec

With the hybrid KV cache manager disabled, _promote_local_kv_cache_specs
rebuilds each SlidingWindowMLASpec as an MLAAttentionSpec via replace_as,
which forwards every field of the source spec. bounded_replay (added in
#56227) exists only on SlidingWindowMLASpec, so the rebuild raises

  TypeError: MLAAttentionSpec.__init__() got an unexpected keyword
  argument 'bounded_replay'

and any sliding-window MLA model (DeepSeek-V4) fails at KV cache planning
under --disable-hybrid-kv-cache-manager. A promoted spec keeps every
block, so the window-bounded replay is moot, as extra_retained_tokens
already is.

Signed-off-by: Basem Barakat <basem.barakay@amd.com>
Co-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>
---
 vllm/v1/core/kv_cache_planning.py | 5 +++--
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/vllm/v1/core/kv_cache_planning.py b/vllm/v1/core/kv_cache_planning.py
index 4d73f4303..2b98d2e9a 100644
--- a/vllm/v1/core/kv_cache_planning.py
+++ b/vllm/v1/core/kv_cache_planning.py
@@ -801,8 +801,9 @@ def _promote_local_kv_cache_specs(
                 spec,
                 target_cls,
                 # Promoted specs allocate blocks for all tokens and never free
-                # below the window, so the trailing-edge extension is moot.
-                drop=("extra_retained_tokens",),
+                # below the window, so the trailing-edge extension and the
+                # window-bounded prefix replay are both moot.
+                drop=("extra_retained_tokens", "bounded_replay"),
                 block_size=block_size,
                 page_size_padded=promoted_page_size_padded(spec, block_size),
             )
